# UI Design Rules

## Responsibilities

- Define visual language and interaction patterns for Legal CRM
- Ensure consistent, premium SaaS appearance across all screens
- Enforce accessibility (WCAG AA), dark mode first, responsive design
- Standardize empty states, skeletons, animations, keyboard shortcuts

## Design Inspiration

| Reference | Adopt |
|-----------|-------|
| **Linear** | Keyboard-first navigation, command palette, subtle animations |
| **Stripe** | Clean data tables, status badges, financial clarity |
| **Attio** | CRM record layouts, relationship views, activity feeds |
| **Notion** | Block-style notes, inline editing, collapsible sections |
| **Vercel** | Dark mode palette, typography hierarchy, minimal chrome |

## Best Practices

- **Dark mode first** — design in dark, verify light mode
- **8px spacing grid** — Tailwind spacing scale (2, 4, 6, 8, 12, 16, 24, 32)
- **Typography**: Inter or Geist Sans; mono for case numbers, IDs
- **Color semantics**: status colors consistent app-wide (see tailwind config)
- **Progressive disclosure** — show essentials, reveal details on demand
- **Command palette** (Cmd+K) for power users
- **Keyboard shortcuts** documented in help modal
- **Micro-interactions** via Framer Motion (150–300ms, ease-out)

## Coding Standards

- Every list view: skeleton loader + empty state + error state
- Forms: inline validation, clear error messages, disabled submit while pending
- Tables: sortable columns, row actions menu, bulk select
- Detail pages: tabbed sections (Overview, Documents, Tasks, Activity)
- Toasts for success/error feedback (sonner)
- Modals for destructive confirmations only

## Folder Structure

```
src/components/
├── layout/         # AppShell, Sidebar, PageHeader, CommandPalette
├── data-display/   # DataTable, StatCard, Timeline, StatusBadge
├── feedback/       # EmptyState, Skeleton*, ErrorFallback
└── forms/          # SearchInput, DateRangePicker, FileUpload

src/features/*/ui/  # Feature-specific views and widgets
```

## Naming Convention

| Element | Pattern |
|---------|---------|
| Page view | *View or *Page | `CasesListView` |
| Widget | *Card, *Panel | `CaseSummaryCard` |
| Skeleton | *Skeleton | `CaseListSkeleton` |
| Empty state | Empty* | `EmptyCases` |
| Modal/Dialog | *Dialog | `DeleteCaseDialog` |

## Performance Rules

- Skeleton loaders match final layout dimensions (no layout shift)
- Animate only `transform` and `opacity` (GPU-accelerated)
- Lazy-load charts and rich text editors
- Reduce motion: respect `prefers-reduced-motion`

## Security Rules

- Mask sensitive data (SSN, account numbers) in UI by default
- Confirm destructive actions with typed confirmation for critical deletes

## Examples

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD — Complete state trinity
export function CasesPage() {
  const { data, isLoading, error } = useCases(filters);
  if (isLoading) return <CasesListSkeleton />;
  if (error) return <ErrorFallback error={error} retry={refetch} />;
  if (!data?.length) return <EmptyCases onCreate={openCreate} />;
  return <CasesList cases={data} />;
}

// ✅ GOOD — Accessible status badge
<Badge variant={statusVariant[case.status]} aria-label={`Status: ${case.status}`}>
  {statusLabel[case.status]}
</Badge>
```

## Things to Avoid

- Inconsistent spacing/padding across pages
- Raw HTML tables without DataTable component
- Flash of unstyled content (missing skeletons)
- Color-only status indicators (always pair with text/icon)
- Blocking modals for non-critical flows
- Generic "No data" without action CTA

## Checklist Before Finishing Any Task

- [ ] Dark mode looks correct
- [ ] Responsive at sm, md, lg, xl breakpoints
- [ ] Loading skeleton implemented
- [ ] Empty state with helpful CTA
- [ ] Error state with retry option
- [ ] WCAG AA contrast ratios met
- [ ] Keyboard navigable (Tab, Enter, Escape)
- [ ] Animations respect reduced-motion preference
